From 52e67bbee2e55996784064d685e6d04de92dd0ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleks <aleks.spv@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:46:51 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 132/194] power: supply: qcom_smbx: Decode the SMB5 charger
 state

SMB5 reorders the states in BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_1 as INHIBIT,
TRICKLE, PRE, FULLON, TAPER, TERMINATE, PAUSE and DISABLE. The charging,
terminate and disable codes agree with SMB2, but inhibit (0) is decoded
as trickle charging and pause (6) as inhibit, i.e. full.

Remap these two states before decoding them.

Signed-off-by: Aleks <aleks.spv@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 019b983fd..aec531949 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -412,6 +412,14 @@ static int smb_get_prop_status(struct smb_chip *chip, int *val)
 
 	stat = stat & BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_MASK;
 
+	/* SMB5 reports inhibit as 0 and pause as 6, the other states match */
+	if (chip->gen == SMB5) {
+		if (stat == 0)
+			stat = INHIBIT_CHARGE;
+		else if (stat == 6)
+			stat = DISABLE_CHARGE;
+	}
+
 	switch (stat) {
 	case TRICKLE_CHARGE:
 	case PRE_CHARGE:
